  'Applications of a computer': {summary:'The chapter describes practical applications of computers in areas such as education, business, communication, healthcare, transport, and public services.',points:['Computers help students learn and teachers prepare learning materials.','Businesses use computers for records, billing, and communication.','Hospitals use computers to maintain patient information and support medical work.','Computers help people communicate and access information.'],activity:'Give students everyday situations and ask which computer application could help.',illustrations:[['📚','Education','Learning resources.'],['🧾','Business','Bills and records.'],['🩺','Healthcare','Patient information.'],['🌐','Communication','Sharing information.']]},
  'Advantages': {summary:'Computers offer several advantages when they are used appropriately.',points:['Speed: computers can process information quickly.','Accuracy: they can produce accurate results when correct data and instructions are supplied.','Storage: they can store large amounts of information.','Diligence: they can repeat tasks without getting tired in the way people do.','Versatility: they can be used for many different kinds of work.'],activity:'Ask students to match speed, accuracy, storage, and versatility with examples from daily life.',illustrations:[['⚡','Speed','Work is completed quickly.'],['🎯','Accuracy','Correct instructions give reliable results.'],['🗄️','Storage','Keep lots of information.'],['🔁','Diligence','Repeat tasks consistently.']]},
